  "invariants": [
    "Reality > Narrative",
    "Evidence > Authority",
    "Capability requires proof",
    "Complexity must earn its existence",
    "Private raw knowledge never becomes shared canon automatically",
    "Operational systems have one truth owner",
    "Providers are adapters, never the PANTHERA core",
    "Legacy sources cannot silently override current canon",
    "No architecture freeze while critical or high freeze-blockers remain",
    "Any active indexed knowledge module must map to a manifest component.",
    "Consent must pass before captured conversation content is transcribed or sent to AI review.",
    "Raw capture material is private source evidence and is never canonical by default.",
    "Raw captures never become canonical knowledge directly.",
    "Consent must pass before any transcript is sent to an external AI reviewer.",
    "Capture authenticity means source provenance/integrity, not factual truth of participant statements.",
    "Raw audio and full transcripts are excluded from canonical Obsidian publications."
